<title>FRANCE: EU seen valuing early-Oct French wheat at $172.22.</title>
<headline>EU seen valuing early-Oct French wheat at $172.22.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union award of 133,350 tonnes of free market soft wheat at a maximum refund of 5.99 Ecus per tonne values a tonne of French wheat for early October shipment at $172.22 per tonne, Reuters calculates.  </p>
<p>The figure, which should be regarded as an estimate only, is based on the following assumptions gathered from market sources and Reuters data.</p>
<p>    Rouen-delivered soft wheat (Oct)   887.50 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    Carrying charge (1st-half Oct)	18.18 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    Fob charges/other charges	     27.50 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    EU refund				    5.99 ecus/tonne</p>
<p>     + EU increment (added to refund)    1.10 ecus/tonne</p>
<p>= Subsidy (at 6.61023 green rate)  46.87 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    Spot franc/dollar			5.1465 francs/dollar</p>
<p>    Implied fob price in dollars	 172.22 dollars/tonne.</p>
<p>The same formula suggests an unsubsidised French fob price of $181.32 per tonne.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
